  "review": [
    "Masks derive from native black/white substitutions, not scan text or a candidate. Fixed source/geometry windows and two-pixel erosion precede fitting. The transparent middle of each paired atlas separates its top/name and bottom/type pigment, consistently for all palettes.",
    "Colorless surround source has70% coverage; a second0.7 pass yields85% coverage, matching the previously reviewed gray title/type treatment. HSB alone could not correct its underlay without clipping. Raw-source policy bypasses pigment and this coverage correction.",
    "All35 clean nonfoil material regions improve in the actual native pipeline; mean OKLab distance x100 falls4.87 to0.53. This color delta is a separate smaller-is-better metric, not the structural accuracy index.",
    "Ugin right-frame sampling is excluded: the scan contains chromatic illustration spilling over the frame. The full card remains in the replay/score denominator. Shared geometry/color fits do not synthesize missing art spill.",
    "Each color has one distinct booster planeswalker name; four blue Teferi art variants are balanced as one name. These are sparse reused-development observations, not independent-name holdouts. The regular blue surround transfers the tall blue pigment to its foil-only deck card.",
    "This completes the foreground material trial, not M21 set certification. Starting-loyalty typography, other remaining component audits, scan-pose certification, final default transfer and release are still open."
  ],
